  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U2"],
      "pins": ["U2.8 (CSB2)"],
      "nets": ["NET0002 (I2C SCL)"],
      "observed": "On the NAVC Peripherals sheet the BMI088 chip-select pin CSB2 (pin 8) is wired to NET0002, the same net that carries the I2C clock (SCL) to every other NAVC-side I2C device (IIS2MDCTR pin 1, TMP100 pin 1, MPRLS0025 pin 2, 24CW1280 pin 1). CSB1 (pin 14) and PS (pin 7) are correctly tied to +3.3V, but CSB2 is not.",
      "expected": "For I2C operation (which the specification states: 'Bosch BMI088, I2C addr 0x19 (acc) / 0x69 (gyr)') both CSB1 and CSB2 must be held at VDDIO/+3.3V. Tying CSB2 to the SCL line means the clock edge toggles the SPI chip-select input, taking the device out of a stable I2C state and corrupting/aborted transfers.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "NAVC Peripherals sheet, U2 BMI088: 'NET0002 -> 8 CSB2' while 'NET0002 -> 1 SCL/SPC' on U6 IIS2MDCTR and 'NET0002 -> 2 SCL/SCL' on U13 MPRLS0025"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "IMU (accel + gyro) ... Bosch BMI088, I2C addr 0x19 (acc) / 0x69 (gyr)"}
      ],
      "impact": "The IMU would not reliably communicate on the I2C bus; accelerometer/gyroscope data (the core navigation input) could be missing or garbled, contradicting the documented I2C addressing.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Most of the build matches the specification (correct MCUs, sensors, regulators, addresses and passive values, with the only documented bug — the barometer RESET/EOC swap — present and excluded). One deviation is visible: the BMI088 CSB2 pin is tied to the I2C SCL net (NET0002) instead of +3.3V, which is inconsistent with the intended I2C operation of the IMU."
}

